    "evidence_text": "Summit County, Ohio\n\nSummit County is an urban county in the U.S. state of Ohio.\n\n Its county seat is Akron.\n\n It was named \"Summit County\" because the highest elevation on the Ohio and Erie Canal is located in the county.\n\nHelena\u2013West Helena, Arkansas\n\nHelena\u2013West Helena is the county seat of and the largest city within Phillips County, Arkansas, United States.\n\n Helena is sited on lowlands between the Mississippi River and the eastern side of Crowley's Ridge.\n\nOld Allamakee County Courthouse (Lansing, Iowa)\n\nJasper County Community Unit School District 1\n\n The principal of Willow Hill is Dave Parker.\n\n Grove Elementary School is located in Island Grove, Illinois, the highest point of elevation in the county.\n\n The district superintendent is Ron Alburtus, and the district's mascot is the eagle.\n\nScapegoat Mountain\n\nGardnerville Branch Jail\n\n Nonetheless, the county approved the construction of the new jail.\n\nMount Jefferson (Nevada)\n\n It is the sixth highest mountain in the state.\n\n For similar reasons, it is also the highest mountain for over 90 miles in all directions.\n\nMcRae\u2013Helena, Georgia\n\n McRae\u2013Helena is the county seat of Telfair County.\n\nHelena, Arkansas\n\nHelena is the eastern portion of Helena-West Helena, Arkansas, a city in Phillips County, Arkansas.\n\nLewis and Clark County, Montana\n\nLewis and Clark County is a county located in the U.S. state of Montana.\n\n Its county seat is Helena, the state capital.\n\n The numerical designation for Lewis and Clark County (used in the issuance of the state's license plates) is 5.",
